Figures from paper
==================

All commands are run from the analyze_embeddings/ directory.

Data and plots are linked via RESULTS_RUN in config.py (e.g. "2025-01-01_000000").
  - Results are read from:  results/<RESULTS_RUN>/
  - Plots are written to:   plots/<RESULTS_RUN>/
After a successful data generation run, update RESULTS_RUN in config.py to point at the new directory.

Prerequisites: run the data generation scripts to produce results in results/<RESULTS_RUN>/:
- python generate_data/evaluate_dpt.py                  -> full_manifold_evaluation.csv, null_manifold_evaluation.csv
- python generate_data/evaluate_stage_permutations.py    -> stage_permutation_specificity.csv
- python generate_data/evaluate_generalizability.py      -> generalizability_results.csv
- python generate_data/hyper_param_sweep.py              -> hyperparam_sweep_k_results.csv, k_sweep_analysis.png
- python generate_data/analyze_trajectory_cellcounts.py  -> crc_conventional_uni2_2000_cellcounts.csv


Main text figures
-----------------

Fig 1: Method overview (SCC progression with diffusion components, pseudotime, tau badge)
  Command: python plotting/plot_method_overview_figure.py --progression SCC
  Output:  plots/method_overview/method_SCC_uni2.png

Fig 2: Trajectory fidelity across foundation models and disease progressions (grouped bars with null baseline)
  Command: python plotting/plot_trajectory_fidelity.py
  Output:  plots/trajectory_fidelity/model_comparison_with_null.png

Fig 3: Averaged permutation test (true ordering vs null distributions pooled across cohorts)
  Command: python plotting/plot_avg_permutation_results.py
  Output:  plots/permutation/permutation_plot_averaged.png

Fig 4: Emergence of trajectory fidelity across network depth (CLS token, 2-panel stacked: tau vs depth + intrinsic dimensionality)
  Command: python plotting/plot_layer_analysis.py
  Output:  plots/emergence/emergence_stacked_cls.png

Fig 5: Cross-task generalization (rank preservation: reference tau predicts held-out F1)
  Command: python plotting/plot_generalizability_test.py
  Output:  plots/generalization/main_panel_b_rank_preservation.png

Fig 6: Biological validation (Z-score standardized cell-type abundance along pseudotime, CRC conventional)
  Command: python plotting/plot_cell_pattern_v2.py --input results/crc_conventional_uni2_2000_cellcounts.csv
  Output:  plots/biological_validation_analysis/standardized_abundance.png


Appendix figures
----------------

Fig 7: Hyperparameter sensitivity (tau and trustworthiness vs k neighbors, 2-panel)
  Command: python generate_data/hyper_param_sweep.py
  Output:  results/<RESULTS_RUN>/k_sweep_analysis.png
  Note:    Generated as part of data generation, not a separate plotting script.

Table 1: Full trajectory fidelity results for all models and progressions with 95% CI
  Command: python plotting/plot_trajectory_fidelity.py
  Output:  plots/trajectory_fidelity/model_progression_trajectory_fidelity.csv

Fig 8: Manifold stability and denoising proof (3-panel: dimensionality compression, spectral gap, fidelity vs trustworthiness)
  Command: python plotting/plot_appendix.py
  Output:  plots/appendix_manifold_robustness.png

Table 2: Aggregated manifold quality metrics (spectral gap, ID reduction, trustworthiness, avg tau)
  Command: python plotting/plot_appendix.py
  Output:  plots/appendix_metrics_table.csv

Fig 9: Per-progression permutation test (2x2 grid, boxplots with true ordering stars)
  Command: python plotting/plot_permutation_results.py
  Output:  plots/permutation/permutation_plot.png

Fig 10: Emergence analysis - patch mean embeddings (3-panel: tau vs relative depth, ID divergence, tau vs absolute block)
  Command: python plotting/plot_layer_analysis.py
  Output:  plots/emergence/emergence_three_panel_patch_mean.png

Fig 11: Emergence analysis - CLS token embeddings (3-panel)
  Command: python plotting/plot_layer_analysis.py
  Output:  plots/emergence/emergence_three_panel_cls.png

Fig 12: Emergence analysis - register mean embeddings (3-panel, DINOv2/UNI-2/Virchow-2 only)
  Command: python plotting/plot_layer_analysis.py
  Output:  plots/emergence/emergence_three_panel_register_mean.png

Fig 13: Within-disease trajectory fidelity vs classification performance (tau vs 5-shot F1 per progression)
  Command: python plotting/plot_generalizability_test.py
  Output:  plots/generalization/main_panel_a_within_disease.png

Fig 14: Trajectory fidelity and classification as equivalent predictors of cross-task generalization (2x4 grid)
  Command: python plotting/plot_generalizability_test.py
  Output:  plots/generalization/appendix_reference_metric_comparison.png

Fig 15: Pseudotime sampling and robustness diagnostics (4 separate plots combined in LaTeX)
  Command: python plotting/plot_cell_pattern_v2.py --input results/crc_conventional_uni2_2000_cellcounts.csv
  Output:  (a) plots/biological_validation_analysis/appendix/pseudotime_density_by_stage.png
           (b) plots/biological_validation_analysis/appendix/pseudotime_density_by_slide.png
           (c) plots/biological_validation_analysis/appendix/pseudotime_local_counts_and_windowN.png
           (d) plots/biological_validation_analysis/appendix/smoothing_robustness_fibroblasts.png

Fig 16: Complete cell type composition along pseudotime (raw proportions + Z-score + stage distribution)
  Command: python plotting/plot_cell_pattern_v2.py --input results/crc_conventional_uni2_2000_cellcounts.csv
  Output:  plots/biological_validation_analysis/appendix/cell_types_zscore_and_raw.png

Fig 17: Pseudotime trajectory sampling with HistoPLUS cell segmentation (patches + overlays + cell proportions)
  Command: python plotting/inspect_trajectory.py --progression CRC-Conventional --model uni2
  Output:  plots/trajectories/trajectory_uni2_CRC-Conventional_prop_seed{SEED}_key.png
           plots/trajectories/trajectory_uni2_CRC-Conventional_prop_seed{SEED}_all.png
  Note:    Requires HistoPLUS (pip install histoplus) and local image data.
           Use --seed to reproduce a specific figure. Without --seed, a random seed is generated.
